  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Through FY2026 to date federal agencies obligated a total of $118M for Other Management Consulting Services, across 497 awards with an average award size of $238K. Obligations fell 86.0% year over year. The Department of Defense led buying with $45.4M, followed by the Department of Health and Human Services with $28.8M and the Department of State with $16.7M. The top vendors so far are ISLAND PEER REVIEW ORGANIZATION INC with $52.4M and PALANTIR USG INC with $22M, while BATTELLE MEMORIAL INSTITUTE accounted for $14.4M and KADIAK LLC for $11.5M. Historical context shows higher spending in prior years: FY24 obligations were $1.3B, FY22 were $913M, and FY21 were $537M, indicating current-year totals are a partial fiscal year picture. Smaller buyers include the Nuclear Regulatory Commission at $1.3M and the Department of the Interior at $1.4M. This mix of large agency demand and a concentrated set of vendors characterizes the market through the current fiscal year to date.",
